From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:15:09 +0300
Subject: ps3fb: release the console's XDR shadow while the RSX driver owns the
 GPU

While an RSX driver (ps3rsx) owns the GPU, ps3fb neither blits nor
flips, and with X in front nobody sees the console, yet the frame part of
ps3fb_videomemory (8 of the default 9 MiB) stays allocated. With
ps3fb.shadow_release=1 (default 0; writable at runtime through
/sys/module/ps3fb/parameters/shadow_release) ps3fb gives it back:

- shadow_release_delay_ms (3000) after ps3fb_gpu_takeover(true), if the
  GPU is still taken and no process has /dev/fbN open: fbcon is suspended
  (fb_set_suspend), screen_base becomes NULL, the frame's IO pages are
  pointed at the first MiB (read only, so a stray GPU fetch never
  faults; if lv1 refuses, nothing is freed), then the memory is freed.
  The first time that is the boot memblock (memblock_phys_free, free_reserved_area: MemTotal
  grows), later the chunks. The state change happens under the lock
  open takes, as fb_read/fb_write check the state unlocked.
- ps3fb_gpu_takeover(false) hands the GPU back at once and queues the
  work, which takes 1 MiB chunks with no lock held (alloc_pages with
  __GFP_NORETRY, else ps3rsx's CMA area), maps them at their IO pages,
  vmaps the first MiB and the chunks for fbcon and resumes fbcon, which
  redraws. Without memory it tries again after 1, 2, 4 ... 32 s.
- The first MiB (reset program, FIFO, the first 512 KiB of the frame)
  stays where it is.

While released the blits, set_par's memset, mmap (-EBUSY) and
PS3GPU_IOCTL_ENTER (-EBUSY) keep off the frame; fbcon, fb_read and
fb_write are gated by FBINFO_STATE_SUSPENDED. Panic output is not drawn
while released, which is no change: with X in front the VT is in
KD_GRAPHICS and ps3fb doesn't blit while the GPU is taken. mmap after the
first release maps the chunks one by one (shared mappings only).
Shutdown unmaps each IO page with what it maps now, and a takeover after
shutdown now returns -ENODEV instead of running the reset program on the
freed context.

With the switch off nothing changes but an open count, a mutex around
mmap and the -ENODEV after shutdown. Compile-tested only; the PS3 test
plan is in docs/KERNEL-MEMORY.md.

Forwarded: no (test on the PS3 first; docs/KERNEL-MEMORY.md)

